          "SRC-008"
        ],
        "description": "The initial alert described a bundled library compiled into the Electron application through Git, while later 3CX and Mandiant reporting identified a trojanized Trading Technologies X_TRADER installer that compromised a 3CX employee system and led into the corporate development and build environment; the supplied evidence preserves both descriptions without resolving them speculatively."
      },
      {
        "contradiction_id": "CONTRA-002",
        "source_references": [
          "SRC-001",
          "SRC-002",
          "SRC-004",
          "SRC-008"
        ],
        "description": "Public reporting described potentially broad exposure of 3CX software used by many organizations, while 3CX and Kaspersky reporting described selective follow-on execution and Gopuram deployment on fewer than ten observed machines; the evidence preserves both the broad-reach and selective-execution propositions without deriving a single victim count."
      }
